<title>SPAIN: Tabacalera sees 200 mln pta gains from Koipe sale.</title>
<headline>Tabacalera sees 200 mln pta gains from Koipe sale.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish tobacco company Tabacalera expects capital gains of 200 million pesetas from the sale of its 9.66 percent stake in olive oil producer Koipe, a member of the board of directors said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The sale price of the stake is 6.2 billion pesetas and its book value is 4.62 billion pesetas, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The company said the deal announced earlier on Wednesday is part of its strategy to concentrate on its core tobacco business and gradually reduce its presence in the food sector.</p>
<p>- Madrid newsroom, 341-585-2160</p>
</text>
